TEXT 0 1104 Left 2 !.include OPA164x/OPA164x.lib
TEXT 0 1136 Left 2 !.ac dec 100 10 100k
TEXT 0 1168 Left 2 ;.op
TEXT 0 1216 Left 2 !.subckt IDEAL_OPAMP inP inN vp vn out\nEin out 0 inP inN 1MEG\nRin_ideal inP inN 1G\n.ends IDEAL_OPAMP
TEXT 0 -112 Left 2 ;RIAA Phono Preamplifier - single channel (schematic version of riaa_preamp.cir)\nTopology: Douglas Self, "Small Signal Audio Design" - single active-stage, non-inverting feedback RIAA equalizer.\nOp-amp: OPA1642 via TI generic OPA164x macromodel (OPA164x/OPA164x.lib, pin order IN+ IN- VCC VEE OUT).\nX1 is drawn flipped vertically (M180) so IN+ is on top: VEE pin at top, VCC pin at bottom.\nLocal "0" = this channel's audio ground; ties to PSU VGND when integrated (see power_supply).
TEXT 0 176 Left 2 ;Cartridge: AT-VM95E (4mV @ 1kHz, 485R, 550mH)\nCload = placeholder total shunt C (target 100-200pF)
TEXT 632 824 Left 2 ;R0/C0: unity DC gain + ~20Hz subsonic pole (~7960us)
TEXT 960 608 Left 2 ;R1*C1 = 3180us (50Hz)\nR2*C2 = 75us (2122Hz)
TEXT 8 1336 Left 2 ;Fallback for pure-topology checks: change X1's Value from OPA164x to IDEAL_OPAMP (supply pins unused by that model).
